<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Chief of the Ma</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Great Chief of the Ma was the title of the leaders of the Meshwesh, Libyan settlers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, during the Third Intermediate Period. Descended from Libyan captives and soldiers settled in the Delta and around Herakleopolis from the twelfth century BCE, such chiefs ruled towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bubastis">Bubastis</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mendes">Mendes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/busiris">Busiris</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shoshenq-i">Shoshenq I</a>, a Great Chief of the Ma, founded the Twenty-second Dynasty around 943 BCE.</p></div>
